1️⃣ Java OutOfMemoryError (OOME)
When it happens
    Java Heap FULL
    AND
    GC cannot reclaim enough memory
    BUT
    Process is still below pod memory limit

    Heap hits Xmx
    ↓
    GC runs (minor / mixed / full)
    ↓
    Still not enough free heap
    ↓
    JVM throws OOME

How it manifests
    App is still running
    ↓
    Request fails
    ↓
    Thread throws exception
    ↓
    App may recover OR degrade

What you see in application logs
    java.lang.OutOfMemoryError: Java heap space
    or
    java.lang.OutOfMemoryError: Metaspace
    or
    java.lang.OutOfMemoryError: unable to create new native thread

What you see in pod status
    State: Running
    Restart Count: unchanged

❗ Pod is NOT restarted automatically (unless your app crashes).

What you see in GC logs
========================
    [Full GC] ... allocation failure
    [GC] ... reclaimed X, still insufficient

    Often followed by:
    java.lang.OutOfMemoryError

What you see in Grafana / Prometheus
JVM metrics
    jvm_memory_used_bytes{area="heap"} ≈ jvm_memory_max_bytes

 Heap Used
 |
 |        ████████████████████  ← flat at Xmx
 |        ████████████████████
 |        ████████████████████
 +----------------------------------> time

 GC metrics
     GC frequency spikes
     GC duration increases
     Throughput drops
     
  Typical causes
  
    Heap leak
    Cache too large
    MaxRAMPercentage too high but still below pod limit
    Metaspace leak (dynamic classloading)